Two fixes for Chiron (is4r-chiron 6.5.4), as chiron-mcp carries them; apply to a checkout
with `git apply chiron-fixes.patch` (or `patch -p1 <`). chiron-mcp applies the same two
at run time in its own process when the Chiron it runs against lacks them
(chiron_mcp/chiron_patches.py); this patch is for Chiron itself, so that its own query
builder gets them too, and for the upstream pull request.

1. CohortDefProcessor._generate_cd_entry_template: a mutable default argument
   (additional_args={}) was returned after being written into, so every filter entry
   built without arguments in one process was the same dict, and building a second
   filter silently rewrote the first (its values, its exclude flag, its entry_id).
   Now a fresh dict per call.

2. The relative-date rule between two event collections ("within 90 days after") read
   each event date straight off the collection table, where a single-value concept
   lives. A dataset loaded with every concept multivalue keeps its dates in lookup
   tables, and the rule failed with AttributeError: <date concept>. The where builder
   now resolves an event date through the subquery's lookup alias (joined like the
   filters' lookups) or, for a table with no subquery of its own, a correlated lookup
   of that record's value (WhereStatementBuilder.get_event_date_column);
   LongitudinalCombo.generate_sql_alchemy_clauses_for_event takes the resolver.

